cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Please also cite the relevant method paper(s) listed under
  "references": Grabec et al. (2024) is the main, most up-to-date
  method reference and should be cited by default. Add Stoklasova
  et al. (2015) as well if you specifically need the half-space
  inverse-procedure discussion or historical attribution, or Grabec
  et al. (2020) if you used Lamb/plate-wave calculations (see each
  reference's "notes" field below). Add the Every et al.
  Green's-function paper as well if you used GreenSolver, regardless
  of which other paper applies.
type: software
title: GuliweRR
version: 6.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
abstract: >-
  Guided Linear Waves by Ritz–Rayleigh — MATLAB and Julia software for
  calculating elastic-wave propagation in anisotropic and layered media,
  with a focus on surface acoustic waves (SAWs). The two implementations
  are kept one-to-one and give the same results.
authors:
  - given-names: Tomas
    family-names: Grabec
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5211-8217"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tomasgrabec/GuliweRR"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24280695
license: ISC
keywords:
  - surface acoustic waves
  - Ritz-Rayleigh method
  - anisotropic elasticity
  - laser ultrasonics
  - guided waves
  - MATLAB
  - Julia
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - given-names: Tomas
        family-names: Grabec
      - given-names: Zuzana
        family-names: Soudná
      - given-names: Kristýna
        family-names: Repček
      - given-names: Klara
        family-names: Lünser
      - given-names: Sebastian
        family-names: Fähler
      - given-names: Pavla
        family-names: Stoklasová
      - given-names: Petr
        family-names: Sedlák
      - given-names: Hanuš
        family-names: Seiner
    title: >-
      Guided acoustic waves in thin epitaxial films: Experiment and
      inverse problem solution for NiTi
    journal: Ultrasonics
    volume: 138
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1016/j.ultras.2023.107211
    notes: >-
      Ritz-Rayleigh method, main paper -- most up-to-date, covers
      layered/film-on-substrate media and the current
      complex-exponential-harmonic formulation, plus the
      inverse-procedure discussion for layered systems. Cite this one
      by default.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - given-names: Tomas
        family-names: Grabec
      - given-names: Petr
        family-names: Sedlák
      - given-names: Hanuš
        family-names: Seiner
    title: >-
      Application of the Ritz-Rayleigh method for Lamb waves in
      extremely anisotropic media
    journal: Wave Motion
    volume: 96
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1016/j.wavemoti.2020.102567
    notes: >-
      Ritz-Rayleigh method extended to Lamb (plate) waves, in the
      earlier real-valued (sin/cos) harmonic formulation -- cite this
      one for plate/Lamb-wave calculations (no updated Lamb-wave
      paper yet).
  - type: article
    authors:
      - given-names: Pavla
        family-names: Stoklasová
      - given-names: Petr
        family-names: Sedlák
      - given-names: Hanuš
        family-names: Seiner
      - given-names: Michal
        family-names: Landa
    title: >-
      Forward and inverse problems for surface acoustic waves in
      anisotropic media: A Ritz-Rayleigh method based approach
    journal: Ultrasonics
    volume: 56
    start: "381"
    end: "389"
    year: 2015
    doi: 10.1016/j.ultras.2014.09.004
    notes: >-
      Original Ritz-Rayleigh paper -- half-space, earlier real-valued
      (sin/cos) harmonic formulation, marginally superseded by Grabec
      et al. (2024). Cite mainly for historical attribution or the
      half-space inverse-procedure discussion.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - given-names: Arthur G.
        family-names: Every
      - given-names: K. Y.
        family-names: Kim
      - given-names: Alexei A.
        family-names: Maznev
    title: >-
      The elastodynamic response of a semi-infinite anisotropic solid
      to sudden surface loading
    journal: Journal of the Acoustical Society of America
    volume: 102
    issue: 3
    start: "1346"
    end: "1355"
    year: 1997
    doi: 10.1121/1.420053
    notes: >-
      Green's-function method -- cite this one in addition to whichever
      Ritz-Rayleigh paper above matches your case, if you used
      GreenSolver.
